          %h2#idea Idea
          %p It is often easier to study formal group schemes using the associated Dieudonne module.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %em Dieudonné module
            is defined to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieudonn%C3%A9+ring"} Dieudonné ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_k
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary"} unitary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+scheme"} group scheme
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            we construct (in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#thmcodir"} Proposition (codir)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M(G)_n:= Hom(G, W_n(k))
            and its limit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi n
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M(G):=lim_n Hom(G, W_n(k))
            become Dieudonné modules.
          %p
            This construction can be executed similarly in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-object"} Ind category
            so we have Dieudonné modules for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group"} formal group
            schemes and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-divisible+groups"} p-divisible groups
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            There is a contravariant equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo .
                  %mi tor
                  %mo .
                  %mi for
                  %mo .
                  %mi Gr
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi k
                  %mo .
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo .
                  %mi fin
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p.tor.for.Gr\simeq D_k .Mod.fin
            between the category of
            = succeed "-torsion" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_k
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#codirected_diagrams_of_witt_modules Codirected diagrams of Witt modules
          .num_prop
            %h6#thmcodir Proposition (codir)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be a perfect field of prime characteristic
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi kRing
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ring
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_n(-):kRing\to Ring
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              assigning to a
              = succeed "-ring" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieudonn%C3%A9+ring"} Dieudonné ring
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi W
                      %mo ̲
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underline W
              be the codirected diagram
            #eq:codir.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mi k
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi V
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi V
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mn 3
                        %mi k
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi V
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{1k}\stackrel{V}{\to}W_{2k}\stackrel{V}{\to}W_{3k}\stackrel{V}{\to}\dots
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo :
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi W
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo →
                              %msub
                                %mi W
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo +
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi …
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ↦
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi …
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V:\begin{cases}W_{n} (k)\to W_{n+1} (k)
                    \\\
                    (x_0,x_1,\dots,x_{n-1})\mapsto (0,x_0,x_1,\dots, x_{n-1})\end{cases}
              denotes the translation.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is sometimes called
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verschiebung+morphism"} Verschiebung morphism
              and satisfies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi VF
                    %mo =
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VF=id
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FV
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FV=p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+morphism"} Frobenius morphism
            %p
              With the multiplication obtained by the algebra map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\hookrightarrow A
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi kRing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in kRing
              and the induced map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)\to W_n(A)\hookrightarrow W(A)
              the above diagram (1) is
              %em not
              a diagram in the category of Dieudonné modules since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is not
              = succeed "-linear" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi λ
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi λ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi p
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(\lambda a)=\lambda^{1/p}T(a)
              hence we have to redefine the multiplication by scalars in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi W
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ×
                              %msub
                                %mi W
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi R
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo →
                              %msub
                                %mi W
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi R
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi a
                              %mo ,
                              %mi w
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ↦
                              %msup
                                %mi a
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi p
                                    %mrow
                                      %mn 1
                                      %mo −
                                      %mi n
                              %mi R
                              %mo ⋅
                              %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    *:\begin{cases}
                    W (k)\times W_{n} (R)\to W_{n} (R)
                    \\\
                    (a,w)\mapsto a^{p^{1-n}} R\cdot w
                    \\end{cases}
            %p
              with this (where we recall that
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi n
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi coker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mi n
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi k
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_n:=coker( T^n:W_k\to W_k)
              = succeed "-linear" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi λ
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi λ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mrow
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %mi n
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi λ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi λ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi n
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi λ
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \displaystyle V(\lambda\star a)=V(\overline{\lambda}^{p^{1-n}}a)=V(F(\overline{\lambda}^{p^{-n}})a)=\overline{\lambda}^{p^{-n}}V(a)=\lambda\star V(a)
          %p
            For an (affine commutative unipotent) group scheme the codirected systems of Witt modules endows the limit of the hom-spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(G,W_n(k))
            with the structure of a Dieudonné module:
          #thmAcu.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "#Demazure"}> III.5
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Acu
                        %mi k
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi Tor
                        %mi V
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mi kMod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Acu_k\simeq Tor_V D_kMod
            %p
              (see also
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+scheme"} group scheme
              for more context concerning this theorem)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+field"} perfect field
              of prime characteristic
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is perfect Frobenius is an automorphism.
            %p
              On the left we have the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine
              commutative
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unipotent+group+scheme"} unipotent group schemes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieudonn%C3%A9+ring"} D_k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieudonn%C3%A9+module"} -modules
              of
              = succeed "-torsion." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo :
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Acu
                                %mi k
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Tor
                                %mi V
                              %msub
                                %mi D
                                %mi kMod
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi G
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi colim
                                %mi n
                              %msub
                                %mi Acu
                                %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi G
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi W
                                %mi nk
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    M:\begin{cases}
                    Acu_k&amp;\to&amp; Tor_V D_kMod
                    \\\
                    G&amp;\mapsto&amp;colim_n Acu_k(G,W_{nk})
                    \\end{cases}
          .proof
            %p
              If we recall that the Dieudonné ring of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+ring"} graded ring
              where the degree
              = succeed "-part" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free module
              generated by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{-n}
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\lt 0
              and by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^n
              if
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\gt 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi colim
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi Acu
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi nk
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim_n Acu_k(G,W_{nk})
              can be multiplied by powers of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              reps. powers of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              by postcomposition.
          %h2#properties_2 Properties
          %p
            Since all the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            operators are are monomorphisms, we get that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(G, W_n(k))\to Hom(G, W_{n+1}(k))
            are all injective and hence we can identify
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(G, W_n(k))
            with a submodule of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(G)
            or explicitly we know that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(G, W_n(k))=\{m \in D(G): V^n(m)=0\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(G)
            is killed by a power of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            If we introduce a bit of abstraction we can see the beauty of all this. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mi Λ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=\Lambda\{F, V\}
            be the noncommutative polynomial ring over the Witt vectors on two indeterminates that satisfy the commutation laws
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fw
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi w
                      %mi p
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fw=w^p F
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi w
                      %mi p
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %mi Vw
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w^p V=Vw
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FV
                    %mo =
                    %mi VF
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FV=VF=p
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Dieudonne ring
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Dieudonne+ring"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(G)
            as a left
            = succeed "-module." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\mapsto D(G)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functor"} contravariant functor
            from affine unitary group schemes to the category of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            torsion. This turns out to be an
